WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.911
My name is Amlesh. This was my first tournament.

2
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:24.671
Three days earlier, the tournament hall felt enormous. I had never played in a place like this before.

3
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:39.309
Aditya played beside me. Rishi taught me. My parents were watching. By the final, Aditya would be across the net.

4
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:48.883
I entered both singles and doubles. Every round made the court feel less unfamiliar.

5
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:04.443
Rishi had taught me to trust the next shot, even when I was unsure of the last one.

6
00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.943
The semifinal put me opposite Rishi, the person who first made me want to play.

7
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:27.652
When the semifinal ended, Rishi smiled first. That made the win feel different.

8
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:36.370
Aditya and I had reached the doubles final together. Now he was my singles opponent.

9
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:47.208
Aditya knew my game better than anyone there. I knew his, too.

10
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.753
Aditya took the first game. I kept searching for a way back into the match.

11
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:10.046
In the second game, I found a rhythm. My feet moved again, and we were even.

12
00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:20.508
Then the cold tightened my legs. The decider began, and I lost its first six points.

13
00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:40.735
Don't play the match to win; play like you enjoy the match.

14
00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:59.784
The next return felt like practice. I stopped counting what I might lose.

15
00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.594
We drew level. Then I moved ahead.

16
00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:17.212
I won the title.

17
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:29.800
But what stayed with me was the joy of playing again.

18
00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.646
For a long time, I thought my father’s advice belonged on the badminton court.

19
00:03:44.353 --> 00:03:48.036
Later, I found the same lesson in Electrical Engineering.

20
00:03:48.759 --> 00:03:50.224
A circuit might fail.

21
00:03:50.713 --> 00:03:52.541
A program might give an error.

22
00:03:53.201 --> 00:03:56.864
Thinking about everything at once could feel overwhelming.

23
00:03:57.489 --> 00:04:01.203
So I learned to focus on the next problem I could solve.

24
00:04:01.937 --> 00:04:05.093
Engineering gave me a place to use that patience.

25
00:04:05.691 --> 00:04:10.195
One point. One circuit. One problem at a time.
